fsgg-coord-engine: KIT DIGEST — a content-addressed kit source is STALE in `registry/repos.lock`:
  .claude/skills/pnext-item
  scripts/fsgg-coord
`repos-registry-selftest` reds `main` until it is regenerated (ADR-0019, #469). Run:
  scripts/repos.sh relock
Then name `registry/repos.lock` as EXPECTED DRIFT in the PR — do NOT reserve it in the
touch-set. It is a GENERATED, CI-GATED artifact, so a collision in it is a REBASE, not a
decision (#309). Reserving it is the three-worker deadlock #527 removed (#428).
  Widen the touch-set (scripts/fsgg-coord widen), or split the PR.
  Fix the PR body now — this is unrecoverable once the PR is merged (editing a merged PR's body does not replay the close, .github#2107).
